    "text": "<p>AC generator-- Converts mechanical energy into electrical energy.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math>.</p><p>Galvanometer--&nbsp;Detects the presence of current in the circuit&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>I</mi></math>.</p><p>Transformer--&nbsp;Changes an alternating voltage for smaller or greater value&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p>Metal detector--&nbsp;Works on the principle of resonance in AC circuit&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math>.</p>"
